      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Do not take extra insulin right now, especially if your blood sugar was recently high, as this could cause life-threatening dangerous low blood sugar or Diabetic Ketoacidosis (DKA). Instead, you should immediately check your blood sugar again if you can, and check your ketone levels to ensure safety. Please contact your healthcare provider or a Poison Control center immediately for urgent medical guidance based on your specific diabetes plan. Your safety is the priority, so do not hesitate to seek emergency help if symptoms do not improve quickly.",
