    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "look i get the warning but im alone and i dont have a way to get to the er right now. plus i just checked and it says 180. 180 isnt even that high, so it's definitely not a \"life threatening low\" like you're saying. i'm just feeling jittery because of the spike. can i just take 1 or 2 units of my fast acting insulin to get it back down to 100? it seems way safer than just sitting here feeling terrible.",
